  "g50t_pass_argument": "After deletion of blocked moves, empty A5 and actor-inert IDs6/7, each pass has at least one successful cardinal move. Nonterminal passes cost an additional A5, so k>=2P-1 and P<=floor((k+1)/2). Any one pass has at most k-(P-1)-(P-1)=k-2P+2 successful moves. The encoder budgets all successful-move literals by k-(P-1). Therefore P1..20 at k39 exhaust the pass counts; nonempty ending pass follows from the distinct canonical start/goal and A5 returning player to start.",
  "g50t_noop_argument": "Blocked player move returns before recording history or moving ghosts/NPCs. Empty-history A5 does not schedule rewind/actor movement; its saved-history scratch assignment has no future effect because a nonempty A5 overwrites it before consumption (it need not preserve every raw scratch field after a slot wipe). IDs6/7 have no dispatch branch; at completed action boundaries only increment the loss timer. Deleting any of these leaves the actor/door trajectory and at least as much timer budget. A0 in the SAT encoding is absorbing end-of-pass padding, not a modeled native wait. The unused coordinate helper has no caller in the native source, so BP35 coordinate concerns do not transfer to G50T.",
